    "Working groups within the MPR are verifying financial records and tax compliance for the two proposed vice presidential candidates.",
    "Constitutional law experts suggest a formal MPR decree is necessary to officially confirm the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
    "The MPR is consulting with various institutions and experts to ensure a legal and orderly process for electing a successor for the remaining term."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia is currently conducting an extensive verification process for two vice presidential candidates proposed by the President. As part of this procedure, MPR working groups have collaborated with the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) to assess wealth reports and consulted with the Ministry of Finance to confirm tax compliance. Concurrently, legal experts and former Constitutional Court (MK) officials are debating the administrative requirements for the transition. There is a strong recommendation from experts that the MPR issue a formal decree (TAP MPR) to finalize the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from his vice-presidential position, citing it as an essential step for accountability. Meanwhile, deliberations continue regarding the upcoming plenary session on December 11, 2026, with an emphasis on prioritizing consensus during the selection of the new vice president.",
